[[File:Energy.png|thumb|220x220px]]
'''Cat Energy''' (also known as just '''Energy''') is one of the [[Upgrade Menu|Upgradable Stats]] in the game, and it is the limit of your playing time. Most levels cost energy to play, except for [[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]], [[Catamin Stages]] and [[Catclaw Dojo]]. If a player does not have enough energy to play a stage, then they need to wait until the energy recharges.

==Recharging Cat Energy==
By default, Cat Energy automatically recharges at a rate of 1 point per minute, which can be reduced to a minimum of 1 point per 30 seconds by obtaining and maxing all [[Treasure#Time Machine|Time Machine Treasures]] in [[Into the Future]]. The player is required to connect to the Internet at least once when playing for the day so the game can sync the time and calculate how much energy a player should have gained correctly. If the player has not done this at all for the day, a warning will appear above the energy count display to tell player about this and the energy will not recharge properly.

Alternatively, players can utilize [[Leadership]]s for an instant energy refill (or 30 [[Cat Food]] if Leaderships are not available). Leaderships can be obtained by clearing a chapter in [[Legend Stages]]/Event Stages, claiming a [[User Rank]] reward or from other sources. This replaces the automatic energy refill mechanic that occurred on such occasions before [[Version 8.2 Update|Version 8.2]]. The amount given is always identical to the player's maximum energy capacity (meaning anything that boosts this capacity will increase the value of each refill) and therefore can overflow. Either way, no more energy can be gained when the player is at or over max energy.

Additionally, there will occasionally be a red button offering a chance to recover energy via an ad. Clicking it will display a prompt with a yes/no choice. Picking yes will play an ad, and finishing the ad will regain 20% of max energy afterwards as a reward. This offer will not appear (or will disappear if already present at first) if the player has at least 80% of their maximum energy. It also can be done only once in a while until it resets after some hours, and the same cooldown applies even if the player declines. However, this does not occur if the player exits during an ad or the selection prompt, similar to the Item Packs in [[Gamatoto Expedition]].

==Increasing Maximum Energy==
Players start off with 100 max energy. The highest max energy is 1200 as of [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]].

Player can increase the maximum energy through multiple ways:
*Upgrading the Cat Energy upgrade using XP. Max at level 10. Increases to level 20 after clearing [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 2. (Total: +190 energy)
*Using Cat Energy upgrade orb from [[Cat Capsule#Normal Cat Capsules|Normal Cat Capsules]]. Enhance +10 levels. (Total: +100 energy)
*Obtaining Management Bible treasures in Empire of Cats; 60 per chapter. (Total: +180 energy)
*Obtaining Future Tech treasures in Into the Future; 30 per chapter. (Total: +90 energy)
*Obtaining Dark Matter treasures in Cats of the Cosmos; 30 per chapter. (Total: +90 energy)
*Clearing all Zombie Outbreak stages in Empire of Cats; 50 per chapter. (Total: +150 energy)
*Clearing all Zombie Outbreak stages in Into the Future; 50 per chapter. (Total: +150 energy)
*Clearing all Zombie Outbreak stages in Cats of the Cosmos; 50 per chapter. (Total: +150 energy)

==Stage Energy Cost==
For this information, please see each stage related pages. Note that the amount of energy required for any stage may change depending on number of clears, stage difficulty or special events. Also take note that the amount of [[XP Function|XP]] earned from completing any stage '''depends''' on their Energy requirement.

Occasionally, a Half Energy Cost event may occur in any of the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]], similar to a [[Treasure Festival]]. Plus, both can occur at the same time, which is very good for farming Treasures.

